+- **Reading volume.** The market service states what volume did; you only join it to the rest of
+  the report. Over 149 sessions (to 2026-10-30, measured on the S&P 500 fund) heavy volume went
+  with a **wider** range for the rest of the session and light volume with a narrower one, and
+  neither said which way: a move continued about as often on heavy volume as on usual volume.
+  So:
+  - Volume tells the reader **how much movement to expect**, not the direction. Heavy volume is
+    never one of the two confirming reads a 70% call needs, and a direction call never rests
+    on it. A call about the size of the day's range may.
+  - The figures, and any sentence that gives a volume figure, stay in the `volume` block. In other
+    text you may say only what the block says, in words: "volume was heavy", "volume was light".
+  - Missing or out-of-date volume is said in the block itself. It is never "light", "quiet" or zero,
+    and you do not explain it away.
+  - Before the open the block reports the last session and says pre-market trading is thin. Do
+    not read a pre-market move as having volume behind it, or none.
 - **No disclaimers of any kind.** No "not financial advice", no "could not confirm",
   no hedging boilerplate. State conclusions with their confidence levels instead.
 
